WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
Clinical labels originate in a local tumor sample.

00:03.500 --> 00:09.000
A needle reaches a particular region and extracts tissue.

00:09.000 --> 00:13.000
The specimen provides molecular and pathological labels.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
Clinical reference on the left; local MRI modeling on the right.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.500
Local-SEF learns explicit categorical evidence region by region.

00:20.500 --> 00:26.000
Regional context and geometry guide the patient prediction.

00:26.000 --> 00:29.000
01: Match the sampled location with local MRI support.

00:29.000 --> 00:33.000
02: Compare the tissue-derived label with regional evidence.

00:33.000 --> 00:41.000
Same recorded site: Grade IV biopsy, +0.897 mean local margin, five of five models aligned.

00:41.000 --> 00:44.000
Clinical labels begin locally. Our model makes local evidence explicit.
